                "_key": "yelo-s-4-b-0-1-s",
                "marks": [
                  "strong"
                ],
                "text": "Yellow only marks the main action and LIVE."
              },
              {
                "_type": "span",
                "_key": "yelo-s-4-b-0-1-s1",
                "marks": [],
                "text": " Event posters are already colourful, a lot of yellow is hard to read, and the old app used a lot of colour at once."
              }
            ],
            "listItem": "bullet",
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "_type": "block",
            "_key": "yelo-s-4-b-1",
            "style": "h3",
            "markDefs": [],
            "children": [
              {
                "_type": "span",
                "_key": "yelo-s-4-b-1-s",
                "marks": [],
                "text": "Status without alarm"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "block",
            "_key": "yelo-s-4-b-2",
            "style": "normal",
            "markDefs": [],
            "children": [
              {
                "_type": "span",
                "_key": "yelo-s-4-b-2-s",
                "marks": [],
                "text": "We tried tinting the sky with service status: green on a busy night, orange or red when there weren’t enough drivers or Yelo wasn’t running. We dropped it because we didn’t want the home screen to scream “the app isn’t working right now”. Service status lives in the small pill that usually says LIVE."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "mediaImage",
            "_key": "yelo-s-4-b-3",
            "localAssetKey": "status",
            "alt": "Three iPhones: Yelo home with a green Busy night for drivers sky, a red Currently not available sky, and the final home with a LIVE pill",
            "caption": "Tried: tinting the sky by service status. Kept: the LIVE pill.",
            "size": "full"
          },
          {
            "_type": "mediaImage",
            "_key": "yelo-s-4-b-4",
            "localAssetKey": "search-live",
            "alt": "A close-up of the Yelo search bar: Where to? with a yellow LIVE pill",
            "caption": "The LIVE pill carries service status.",
            "size": "full"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "projectSection",
        "_key": "yelo-section-5",
        "title": "Onboarding",
        "heading": "Sign-up that gets you riding",
        "content": [
          {
            "_type": "block",
            "_key": "yelo-s-5-b-0",
            "style": "normal",
            "markDefs": [],
            "children": [
              {
                "_type": "span",
                "_key": "yelo-s-5-b-0-s",
                "marks": [],
                "text": "The final sign-up has seven short steps: welcome, phone number, a text code, student status, a pre-filled profile, an optional photo and permissions."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "mediaImage",
            "_key": "yelo-s-5-b-1",
            "localAssetKey": "onboarding-1",
            "alt": "Three iPhones: the Yelo welcome screen, the phone number step and Claim your student status with Google or Microsoft",
            "caption": "Welcome, phone number, student status.",
            "size": "full"
          },
          {
            "_type": "block",
            "_key": "yelo-s-5-b-2-0",
            "style": "normal",
            "markDefs": [],
            "children": [
              {
                "_type": "span",
                "_key": "yelo-s-5-b-2-0-s",
                "marks": [
                  "strong"
                ],
                "text": "Phone first."
              },
              {
                "_type": "span",
                "_key": "yelo-s-5-b-2-0-s1",
                "marks": [],
                "text": " Your phone number is your login, drivers need to reach you, and it’s the quickest way to start. It was also a requirement from the founders."
              }
            ],
            "listItem": "bullet",
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "_type": "block",
            "_key": "yelo-s-5-b-2-1",
            "style": "normal",
            "markDefs": [],
            "children": [
              {
                "_type": "span",
                "_key": "yelo-s-5-b-2-1-s",
                "marks": [
                  "strong"
                ],
                "text": "School Google or Microsoft sign-in"
              },
              {
                "_type": "span",
                "_key": "yelo-s-5-b-2-1-s1",
                "marks": [],
                "text": " replaced the old school picker. It’s fewer steps, most students already have one of those accounts, it keeps Yelo students-only, and it fills in the profile. An emailed code is still there as a fallback."
              }
            ],
            "listItem": "bullet",
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "_type": "block",
            "_key": "yelo-s-5-b-2-2",
            "style": "normal",
            "markDefs": [],
            "children": [
              {
                "_type": "span",
                "_key": "yelo-s-5-b-2-2-s",
                "marks": [
                  "strong"
                ],
                "text": "The welcome screen shows the app,"
              },
              {
                "_type": "span",
                "_key": "yelo-s-5-b-2-2-s1",
                "marks": [],
                "text": " with the feed, events and deals, so the social side is clear before you sign up and Yelo doesn’t read as just another ride-share."
              }
            ],
            "listItem": "bullet",
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "_type": "mediaImage",
            "_key": "yelo-s-5-b-3",
            "localAssetKey": "onboarding-2",
            "alt": "Three iPhones: the pre-filled Yelo profile, the optional profile picture step, and permissions with a reason for each",
            "caption": "Pre-filled profile, optional photo, permissions.",
            "size": "full"
          },
          {
            "_type": "block",
            "_key": "yelo-s-5-b-4-0",
            "style": "normal",
            "markDefs": [],
            "children": [
              {
                "_type": "span",
                "_key": "yelo-s-5-b-4-0-s",
                "marks": [
                  "strong"
                ],
                "text": "Confirm, don’t type."
              },
              {
                "_type": "span",
                "_key": "yelo-s-5-b-4-0-s1",
                "marks": [],
                "text": " The profile comes pre-filled from the school account."
              }
            ],
            "listItem": "bullet",
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "_type": "block",
            "_key": "yelo-s-5-b-4-1",
            "style": "normal",
            "markDefs": [],
            "children": [
              {
                "_type": "span",
                "_key": "yelo-s-5-b-4-1-s",
                "marks": [
                  "strong"
                ],
                "text": "The photo is optional for riders"
              },
              {
                "_type": "span",
                "_key": "yelo-s-5-b-4-1-s1",
                "marks": [],
                "text": " and only used in social features. Drivers have to add one. Fewer required steps means fewer people drop off."
              }
            ],
            "listItem": "bullet",
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "_type": "block",
            "_key": "yelo-s-5-b-4-2",
            "style": "normal",
            "markDefs": [],
            "children": [
              {
                "_type": "span",
                "_key": "yelo-s-5-b-4-2-s",
                "marks": [
                  "strong"
                ],
                "text": "Every permission says why."
              },
              {
                "_type": "span",
                "_key": "yelo-s-5-b-4-2-s1",
                "marks": [],
                "text": " Reasons build trust, especially for contacts."
              }
            ],
            "listItem": "bullet",
            "level": 1
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "projectSection",
        "_key": "yelo-section-6",
        "title": "Outcome",
        "heading": "What shipped",
        "content": [
          {
            "_type": "block",
            "_key": "yelo-s-6-b-0",
            "style": "normal",
            "markDefs": [],
            "children": [
              {
                "_type": "span",
                "_key": "yelo-s-6-b-0-s",
                "marks": [],
                "text": "Home and feed, search and map, ride options and onboarding are live."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "block",
            "_key": "yelo-s-6-b-1",
            "style": "h3",
            "markDefs": [],
            "children": [
              {
                "_type": "span",
                "_key": "yelo-s-6-b-1-s",
                "marks": [],
                "text": "What I learned"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "block",
            "_key": "yelo-s-6-b-2-0",
            "style": "normal",
            "markDefs": [],
            "children": [
              {
                "_type": "span",
                "_key": "yelo-s-6-b-2-0-s",
                "marks": [
                  "strong"
                ],
                "text": "Old habits inform design."
              },
              {
                "_type": "span",
                "_key": "yelo-s-6-b-2-0-s1",
                "marks": [],
                "text": " People already reacted to each other’s ride requests in the iMessage version, and that’s where reactions came from."
              }
            ],
            "listItem": "bullet",
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "_type": "block",
            "_key": "yelo-s-6-b-2-1",
            "style": "normal",
            "markDefs": [],
            "children": [
              {
                "_type": "span",
                "_key": "yelo-s-6-b-2-1-s",
                "marks": [
                  "strong"
                ],
                "text": "Booking first, social second."
              },
              {
                "_type": "span",
                "_key": "yelo-s-6-b-2-1-s1",
                "marks": [],
                "text": " Social signals only help if they don’t slow down getting a ride."
              }
            ],
            "listItem": "bullet",
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "_type": "block",
            "_key": "yelo-s-6-b-2-2",
            "style": "normal",
            "markDefs": [],
            "children": [
              {
                "_type": "span",
                "_key": "yelo-s-6-b-2-2-s",
                "marks": [
                  "strong"
                ],
                "text": "Simplify a crowded home."
              },
              {
                "_type": "span",
                "_key": "yelo-s-6-b-2-2-s1",
                "marks": [],
                "text": " A lot of the work was deciding what to leave out, like reaction counts and the status-tinted sky."
              }
            ],
            "listItem": "bullet",
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "_type": "block",
            "_key": "yelo-s-6-b-3",
            "style": "h3",
            "markDefs": [],
            "children": [
              {
                "_type": "span",
                "_key": "yelo-s-6-b-3-s",
                "marks": [],
                "text": "Summary"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "block",
            "_key": "yelo-s-6-b-4",
            "style": "normal",
            "markDefs": [],
            "children": [
              {
                "_type": "span",
                "_key": "yelo-s-6-b-4-s",
                "marks": [],
                "text": "Yelo’s earlier app was live, but its home was crowded, social features felt bolted on, and the look was dated. I explored four home directions, and the founders went with B’s layout, combined with parts of A, so booking stays first."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "block",
            "_key": "yelo-s-6-b-5",
            "style": "normal",
            "markDefs": [],
            "children": [
              {
                "_type": "span",
                "_key": "yelo-s-6-b-5-s",
                "marks": [],
                "text": "I reworked the feed cards so mixed card types are easy to scan. I swapped Exclusive and Shared for named vehicle classes that match the real fleet. And sign-up got shorter, with a profile that fills itself in from your school account. Search now sits at the top of home, and the feed underneath shows where people are headed, who got tickets and what’s trending."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
